  <content>
    <procedure>
      <preliminaryRqmts>
        <reqCondGroup>
          <reqCondNoRef>
            <reqCond>Aircraft electrically safe for maintenance.</reqCond>
          </reqCondNoRef>
          <reqCondNoRef>
            <reqCond>Radome access permitted by the applicable maintenance configuration.</reqCond>
          </reqCondNoRef>
          <reqCondNoRef>
            <reqCond>Weather-radar system de-energized before access to the radome area.</reqCond>
          </reqCondNoRef>
        </reqCondGroup>

        <reqPersons>
          <person man="1"/>
        </reqPersons>

        <reqSupportEquips>
          <noSupportEquips/>
        </reqSupportEquips>

        <reqSupplies>
          <noSupplies/>
        </reqSupplies>

        <reqSpares>
          <noSpares/>
        </reqSpares>

        <safety>
          <warning>
            <warningAndCautionPara>
              Make sure that the weather-radar system is de-energized before you open or
              work near the radome area. Radio-frequency exposure can cause injury.
            </warningAndCautionPara>
          </warning>
          <caution>
            <warningAndCautionPara>
              Do not use metallic tools, abrasive materials, or unauthorized solvents on
              lightning diverter paths, radome laminate, or bonding provisions. Damage to
              these areas can reduce lightning and radio-frequency performance.
            </warningAndCautionPara>
          </caution>
        </safety>
      </preliminaryRqmts>

      <mainProcedure>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>
            Get access to the radome external surface and the radome-to-backup-structure
            bonding interface in accordance with the applicable access procedure.
          </para>
        </proceduralStep>

        <proceduralStep>
          <para>
            Do a visual check of the lightning diverter paths and adjacent radome surface.
          </para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check for missing, loose, lifted, cracked, burned, or contaminated diverter elements.</para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check for erosion, blistering, cracking, delamination, or moisture ingress near the diverter paths.</para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check for evidence of lightning attachment, arc tracking, puncture, or thermal damage.</para>
            </listItem>
          </randomList>
        </proceduralStep>

        <proceduralStep>
          <para>
            Do a visual check of radome-side bonding provisions at the attachment boundary.
          </para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check that bonding straps, bonding lands, fastener interfaces, or bonding points are correctly seated.</para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check for corrosion, contamination, loose hardware, missing hardware, or damaged contact surfaces.</para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>Check that seals and drainage provisions do not obstruct the bonding path.</para>
            </listItem>
          </randomList>
        </proceduralStep>

        <proceduralStep>
          <para>
            If the applicable maintenance programme requires an electrical continuity check,
            measure the bonding continuity using approved test equipment and limits from the
            lightning-protection system publication.
          </para>
          <note>
            <notePara>
              Bonding resistance limits are owned by the lightning-protection system and are
              not defined in this radome publication.
            </notePara>
          </note>
        </proceduralStep>

        <proceduralStep>
          <para>
            If damage, contamination, loss of bonding continuity, or suspected lightning
            attachment is found, record the finding and refer to the applicable lightning
            protection, structural inspection, and engineering disposition procedures.
          </para>
        </proceduralStep>
      </mainProcedure>

      <closeRqmts>
        <reqCondGroup>
          <reqCondNoRef>
            <reqCond>All access panels, radome latches, seals, and local bonding provisions returned to the required maintenance configuration.</reqCond>
          </reqCondNoRef>
          <reqCondNoRef>
            <reqCond>Findings recorded in the applicable maintenance and evidence system.</reqCond>
          </reqCondNoRef>
        </reqCondGroup>
      </closeRqmts>
    </procedure>
  </content>
</dmodule>
